  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Early Childhood Development Education (ECDE) upscale in Homa Bay County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This task order builds on the TO20 -Early Childhood Development Education (ECDE) in Kenya - which was implemented during the innovation phase of the DID proramme. The evidence generated in TO20, which ended in December 2023, confirms that training and support for both teachers and parents is an essential as it gives both groups the confidence to try inclusion in practice, in their classes or with their own child at home/in the community respectively. It also confirms that providing awareness raising with a variety of different stakeholders in the community as well as discussing this with government educationalists and policy makers at different levels, and other service providers such as health workers, assessment centres and advisors is essential. The overall plan to scale up the intensive work that has been done under TO20 in 6 schools in Homa Bay county aims at children with and without disabilities will have access to materials that will support their learning and development in 80 schools (2 in every ward) across the county. By working  through the ward system, The eventually trained more than 40 key education service providers will have been trained in simple and effective strategies  for becoming more inclusive and engaging with young children using effective pedagogies. The teachers will have been trained in developing teaching  and learning play materials from locally available materials enabling the enrichment of the classroom with play materials. These education service providers will cascade the training to teachers in their wards thus building capacity of teachers across the county. Teachers will have access to  resources and ideas about how to increase learning through involving children in structured and non-structured play. An open-access package to support inclusion of children with disabilities in curriculum delivery, social and environmental accessibility will be developed. As early childhood education is devolved at county level in Kenya, the intervention will be introduced to the Council of Governors, a platform that brings together all the 47  county leaders in Kenya. The initiative aligns well with the Homa Bay County education policy priorities as proposed in the County Intergrated Development Plan (CIDP) 2023-2027 (influenced by OPDs under TO20), with a focus on quality, relevant and inclusive education to promote social cohesion and sustainably developing ways of making ECDE inclusive and accessible to all learners. It responds to national education policy priorities drawn in the Kenya National Education Sector Plan 2023-2027 as well as the Kenya National Vision for Education which prioritizes free basic education, enhancing education quality and relevance. This task order covers phase 1 of the upscale work on TO20, from January to December 2025. Phase 2 will be implemented outside the DID programme from January 2026 onwards.</narrative>
  </description>
